    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d219">

                <pb facs="0335" n="265" xml:id="pg265"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Stuart.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-06-24"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 24, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have been informally apprised that Mr.
                    Coppell, her Britannic Majesty’s acting consul at New Orleans, has deemed it
                    advisable to relinquish his official functions in consequence of a letter
                    addressed to him by Major General Butler, issued, it is presumed, through some
                    misapprehension. I do not think the facts of the case justified General Butler
                    in writing that letter. I will thank you, therefore, to request that gentleman
                    to resume his consular character, the supposed cause of the abandonment of which
                    is regretted. The Secretary of War has been requested to issue proper orders
                    upon the subject to General Butler.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your very obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William Stuart, </hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
